[remap]

; importer="keep", NOT "csv_translation" — and this one line is why an iOS build showed UI_NEW_WORLD
; instead of "new world" for every string in the game.
;
; With the csv_translation importer Godot treats this file as the SOURCE of an imported resource. The
; exporter then ships only the generated .translation binary and strips the .csv itself. In the editor
; that is completely invisible, because the source file is sitting right there on disk; in an exported
; build FileAccess.open() returns null, Locale registers zero translations, and tr() falls through to
; the raw key for every label and button.
;
; "keep" tells Godot to import nothing and copy the file verbatim, so the CSV the Locale autoload
; parses at runtime is genuinely present in the package. See scripts/core/locale.gd for why this
; project parses the CSV itself rather than using the engine's translation pipeline.
importer="keep"
